Author: Devuser <hi@devuser.nu>
Date:   Sat Jul 11 20:11:42 2026 +0200

    feat(feed): wire retrieve's date/source/type/tag filters and coverage

    Agents calling retrieve need to actually narrow a query and to tell a
    quiet feed day apart from a broken scan, not just see inert echo
    fields left by the prior slice. Filters now shape the chunk query
    (reusing search-chunks' proven parsing, with retrieve staying
    unbounded by default so a mandate-blind full-corpus call is never
    silently narrowed), and per-provider coverage is on by default and
    always present, even for a zero-hit response.

